## Revision delta from revision 6: integrity repair

Revision 6 passed its cross-stage review before the gate wrote its verdict, but the revision-6 manifest had hashed the prior r5 verdict at the mutable canonical path `verdict_investigation-review.cross-stage.json`. The gate wrote the new r6 verdict to that same path, replacing the bytes that the r6 manifest referenced. A post-verdict boundary check therefore reported a stale artifact hash. The r6 verdict itself has been preserved byte-for-byte for lineage.

Revision 7 removes that mutable canonical verdict path from its artifact hashes and evidence-chain inputs, and binds the immutable r6 verdict archive instead. This repairs the evidence binding only; it does not alter the technical findings or diagnostic plan. AC-4 remains failed, and no new capture, test, product source change, or AC-4 fix occurred.

## Finding and bounded BUILD path

The accepted five-minute current-source reproduction remains 6,050 matched frames over 302.506666 seconds, mean 20.000523 fps, maximum EOF gap 89.163715 ms, and 753/6,049 gaps above 60 ms. This fails AC-4's maximum-gap criterion. The evidence localizes jitter after V4L2 dequeue and before raw-pipe delivery inside FFmpeg processing/output, but the exact internal wait/processing cause remains unresolved. PTS are V4L2 SOE, not EOF; keep `timestampEof` as host-monotonic time sampled after each complete raw-frame read.

**Owner:** BUILD through `build/build-management`, only after revision 7 is approved.

If approved, run one 600-frame diagnostic on the same assigned camera using the fixed FFmpeg executable and unchanged default production argv. Keep the 1280×720 MJPEG-to-NV12 mode, one decoder thread, one filter thread, queue size 1, the same camera, and the same reader. Save no frame payload. After startup, arm a one-shot monotonic watchdog for each in-flight full-frame read; if it remains incomplete for more than 60 ms, take at most one GDB snapshot for that read. Re-arm only after that frame completes; allow at most three snapshots total. Verify the target PID is the live FFmpeg child and `/proc/<pid>/exe` plus its command line match the fixed executable and expected argv. Use `gdb --quiet --batch --nx --pid <pid>` with pagination and confirmation off, debuginfod disabled, `info threads`, `thread apply all bt 16`, then detach and quit. Record monotonic trigger, attach, detach, and full-read-completion times, debugger pause duration, and TID/LWP mapping. Do not use `strace` or another tracer. Abort and clean up if PID verification, attach, backtrace collection, or detach fails.

GDB stops FFmpeg threads while collecting each snapshot, so these pauses perturb cadence and may extend each triggering gap. The snapshots are for callsite localization only; their timings cannot measure AC-4 and do not establish causality. This step is diagnostic only, makes no source or argv change, and does not replace a separate accepted five-minute AC-4 run.

